   "title": "Bombardier, CRJ100/200/440 Airport Planning Manual (CSP A-020, Revision 8, Jan 10/2016), 00-02-01: Figure 2 General Airplane Dimensions (Metric), Figure 3 Ground Clearances, Figure 10 Passenger Door and Service Door Clearances, Figure 11 Cargo Compartment Door Clearance",
   "accessed": "2026-11-16",
   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off Figure 2's side, plan and front views (tools/trace/crj2/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. Figure 2 is a binarized scan; its side and plan are drawn to one scale (the plan's printed 9.30 m wing and 4.27 m root chord within 0.5%), its front view 1.7% larger (by its printed 21.23 m span), rendered to the side's scale. The side view is drawn level. Scaled by the printed 24.38 m fuselage length. A T-tail (the tailplane on the fin's top fairing, which runs aft to a point over the tailplane's tips: the printed 26.77 m overall length) with winglets and two CF34-3 nacelles on stub pylons on the rear fuselage. The plan draws the tailplane 3.0% wider than its printed 6.20 m (the front view 1.1%): the shape keeps the plan's. The front view draws the nacelle's inlet ring 1.40 m wide and 1.44 m tall against the printed 1.45 m (its own dimension lines 1.42 m apart; the plan's nacelle 1.33 m across by line centres): the shape keeps the drawing's ring (-3.8%). The side view draws the passenger door 0.97 m wide by line centres against the printed 0.91 m (the opening). The side view draws the 13 cabin windows a side, the passenger door (left) and the Type III overwing exit (both sides, Figure 3). The right side's galley service door is placed from Figure 10's dashed outline, relative to the passenger door. The cargo door (left side, 1.09 by 0.84 m opening) isn't drawn on Figure 2: Figure 11's plan sketch puts it from FS578 to FS621, just behind the nacelle's inlet lip (about FS577), so it's placed from 0.03 m behind the lip; its sill at the passenger door's (Figure 3's B and D both reach 1.73 m above the ground). All other checks within 0.7%. The manual covers the CRJ100, CRJ200 and CRJ440 (CL-600-2B19), one airframe: the shape serves CRJ1 too."
  }
